  "obligation": "Bind binary functions/imports/indirect-call expectations to declared type identity and compare actual callable types by recursive equivalence and declared ancestry across original instance/program owners.",
  "representation": "WasmCallableType is Declared(source type index) or Embedded(explicit signature). The pool retains declaration identity and memoizes its supported machine-value signature once. Declared entries intern by whole-group equivalence, not shape equality; embedding signatures model final singleton function types. Imported/native function matching and indirect target matching share wasm_callable_matches and the same pool operations. Function cells retain their original program, function index and captured environment through imports/re-exports; no forwarding or retagging. Non-final/grouped scalar callable types now execute with identity retained. Shared/descriptor/continuation types and concrete/non-null value types remain explicitly unsupported. The frontend duplicate signature conversion and unused ProgramStore projection are removed; lowering derives one temporary signature per body instead of copying every signature into another table. No opcode, Value/cell, executor or format change. Rust embedding fixtures now name their explicit Embedded input; pinned guest cases/expectations are unchanged.",
